{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_chapter12a", "label": "Chapter 12A \u2014 The shape, a cylinder over the transfer", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_cylinder_not_mobius", "label": "\u039b is orientable \u2014 a cylinder, not a M\u00f6bius band", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The sign structure is bipartite, and a bipartite structure can never produce an odd number of orientation reversals; both routes to a M\u00f6bius band are closed, so this is a reason rather than an absence of evidence."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_lach_cylinder", "label": "The Lach Cylinder \u2014 a hydrogenic cylinder over \u03bd, and over the transfer", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Over,' not 'graded by': \u03bd grades every chain of \u039b but grades \u039b itself nowhere, and the bracket of Part V operates along chains because that is exactly where \u03bd is a grading."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_fibration_two_body", "label": "The cylinder is a fibration, and its fibres are two-body", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_conditional_factorisation", "label": "It does not factorise, and then it does \u2014 |\u039b| = \u03a3_q |A(q)|\u00b7|B(q)| = 976", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "As a bare product it fails at 2,244 against 976 because the two ends are coupled twice over; conditioned on the coupling they separate exactly, the way a two-body problem separates into centre-of-mass and relative motion."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_fibre_profile", "label": "The cylinder's profile \u2014 cross-sections 165, 330, 345, 136", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_pareto_frontier", "label": "A Pareto frontier inside the lattice \u2014 raising the transfer costs the parent and pays the target", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_most_probable_transfer", "label": "A most-probable transfer \u2014 peak at q = 2, \u27e8q\u27e9 = 1.4631", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_cross_section_closure", "label": "Every cross-section is itself closed \u2014 E(A_q) = E(B_q) = 0 for every q", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This does not follow from \u039b being closed: a closed index could in principle have defective slices that cancel in the total. Here none do, which makes it a new invariant."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_compression_eight_to_three", "label": "An eight-to-three compression that loses no count", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It forgets which coordinate inside each side and keeps how many \u2014 a general fact about caterpillars, which reduce to (base, left, right) whatever their length."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_interval_box_condition", "label": "When an interval is a box \u2014 27% of random intervals qualify", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_maximal_chains", "label": "Maximal chains \u2014 e(P) = 1,113,045,672 linear extensions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_ninth_axis_2s_prime", "label": "The ninth axis 2S\u2032 \u2264 g \u2014 an axis the index did not carry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Never a closure defect (the reconstruction cannot see a coordinate never supplied) but an axis the extension admits, made visible by the asymmetry of the two fibres. Built by the identical rule as the parent's spin bound."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_figure_12_1", "label": "Figure 12.1 \u2014 the object as a cylinder", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_figure_12_2", "label": "Figure 12.2 \u2014 cross-sections of the tower cylinder at each transfer", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_chapter12a", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_cylinder_not_mobius", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_chapter12a", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_lach_cylinder", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_chapter12a", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_fibration_two_body", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter12A-shape.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_chapter12a", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter12a_shape_conditional_factorisation", "relation": "references", "confidenc